  ('sum', 'O(n)', 'sum a list', 'One pass, constant work per element.'),
  ('swap-ends', 'O(1)', 'swap first and last', 'A fixed number of reads and writes. No step walks the array.'),
  ('three-sum', 'O(n²)', 'three numbers summing to zero', 'Sorting is O(n log n), then n two-pointer sweeps of O(n) each, which gives O(n²) overall.'),
  ('to-binary', 'O(log n)', 'number to binary string', 'One bit is produced per iteration, and n has about log₂ n bits.'),
  ('triangles', 'O(n³)', 'count triangles in an adjacency matrix', 'In the worst case (a dense graph), every vertex triple i < j < k is examined.'),
  ('triangular-below', 'O(√n)', 'triangular numbers up to n', 'The k-th triangular number is about k² / 2, so the loop ends after about √(2n) steps.'),
  ('tsp-brute', 'O(n!)', 'shortest round trip by brute force', 'It tries all (n − 1)! orders of the other cities and prices each one in O(n).'),
